course: dictionary
lesson: 15269
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the writer wants. «The letter sigma comes after rho in the Greek alphabet.» The words Greek alphabet are the clue, so sigma means a letter here.
explain: «The sum Σ of 2 to 4 is 9, because 2 + 3 + 4 = 9.» The clue is sum and the numbers, so Σ means add up all of these. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Slang meanings change from place to place and year to year. «My cousin said her friend is so sigma because he never copies anyone.» The clue is never copies anyone, so sigma means cool and independent here. Some people use it as a joke, so if you are unsure, ask an adult.
fact: Sigma is the eighteenth letter of the Greek alphabet.
fact: The capital letter Σ is used in maths to mean add up all of these.
fact: The small letter σ is used in statistics for standard deviation, which shows how spread out numbers are.
fact: «Sigma» as slang means cool or independent, and it is a meme word, not a maths word.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The eighteenth letter of the Greek alphabet is sigma.» What is sigma in this sentence? | A kind of cake | A type of car | A number on a clock | *A letter
exercise: In the sum «Σ of 1 to 4», what does Σ tell you to do? | Multiply the numbers together | *Add up all the numbers from 1 to 4 | Draw a circle round the 4 | Take 4 away from 1
exercise: «He is a sigma, he does his own thing.» In this sentence, sigma means: | A sleepy animal | *Cool and independent | Very old | A Greek letter used in a sum
test: The sum Σ of 1 to 3 is which number? | *6 | 3 | 4 | 9
test: In statistics, the small letter σ is used for what? | The total of all the numbers | *How spread out numbers are | The colour of a graph | The number of letters in a word
exam: In the sum Σ of 2 + 3 + 4, sigma means which of these? | *Add up all of these | A Greek letter for a city | Very old | Slang for hungry
